        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "If \\(\\\\lvert\\\\vec a\\\\rvert=3\\), \\(\\\\lvert\\\\vec b\\\\rvert=4\\), and the angle between \\(\\\\vec a\\) and \\(\\\\vec b\\) is \\(60^\\\\circ\\), then \\(\\\\lvert2\\\\vec a-\\\\vec b\\\\rvert\\) equals",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "\\(\\\\lvert2\\\\vec a-\\\\vec b\\\\rvert^2=4\\\\lvert\\\\vec a\\\\rvert^2+\\\\lvert\\\\vec b\\\\rvert^2-4\\\\vec a\\\\cdot\\\\vec b\\). Since \\(\\\\vec a\\\\cdot\\\\vec b=3\\\\cdot4\\\\cos60^\\\\circ=6\\), the squared magnitude is \\(36+16-24=28\\). Therefore the answer is \\(\\\\sqrt{28}=2\\\\sqrt7\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
